3. CORE THIRD-PARTY RUST DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

Both the client engine (`Cargo.toml`) and the zero-plaintext control plane
(`cloud/Cargo.toml`) incorporate the following core open-source Rust crates
(verified against Cargo.lock; licenses summarized below):

- `rusqlite` (0.32) & SQLite (`libsqlite3-sys` 0.30)
  License: MIT (`rusqlite`) / Public Domain (embedded SQLite)
  Local-first encrypted vault storage and control-plane metadata persistence.

- `axum` (0.8)
  License: MIT
  HTTP router and stateless ZDR API gateway for `qi-cloud`.

- `ed25519-dalek` (2.2)
  License: BSD-3-Clause
  Ed25519 signing and offline verification of OSET entitlement tokens.

- `chacha20poly1305` (0.10)
  License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  Client-side XChaCha20-Poly1305 authenticated encryption for E2EE sync shards.

- `rustls` (0.23), `ring` (0.17) & `rustls-webpki` (0.103)
  Licenses:
  - `rustls`: Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT
  - `ring`: Apache-2.0 AND ISC (no legacy OpenSSL/SSLeay advertising clause)
  - `rustls-webpki`: ISC
  TLS transport security and StoreKit 2 X.509 certificate-chain / ECDSA P-256
  cryptographic signature verification.

- `chrono` (0.4)
  License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  Timestamps, solar-term calendar windows, and biometric cycle alignment.

- `serde` (1.0)
  License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  Structured JSON serialization across native modules, sync envelopes, and cloud APIs.

- `ureq` (2.12)
  License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  Blocking HTTPS client for ZDR AI gateway and WebDAV/control-plane requests.

